<p>Brazil’s Supreme Federal Court has convicted four men for the 2018 assassination of Rio de Janeiro city councilor Marielle Franco and her driver, Anderson Gomes. Two brothers with political influence in Rio de Janeiro—former congressman João Francisco “Chiquinho” Brazão and Domingos Inácio Brazão—were found guilty of ordering the murders and each received a sentence of 76 years and three months in prison; several outlets described the decision as unanimous. The court also convicted two former police officers, according to reporting.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/eJJTBLwx9Ou7ikg7rc1uREWcBHyzbGPijbjm8sNYgTueRr3RNRGSLX9T3X6Ju4vq3-xRn_kYG6zmeIcG4lT8U0DuU3tpDUQBj7D_whQSetEEyJuS-yDAkeErYjRffrtg1I1WvE4KlBwc_wsuRqIg3W_y8bmCgmYn2Xg0mh4U8IbgJvm7fzJFSeLVEkAqo6WIbdPpn9ZosTlo1LhjBxldzEfu2M8' alt='Marielle Franco, a member of Rio de Janeiro’s City Council, leading a session in 2017 at the municipal chamber in Rio de Janeiro.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Charges cited: France 24 said the court convicted the Brazão brothers of double aggravated homicide, participation in an armed criminal organization, and attempted murder.</li><li>Paramilitary links: El País described the brothers as political strongmen who defended the interests of paramilitary criminal groups in Rio de Janeiro.</li><li>Victims remembered: The Guardian noted Franco was a gay Black woman and rising political figure in Rio, and Gomes was 39 when he was killed.</li><li>Public response: The BBC reported Franco’s murder at age 38 sparked protests across Brazil and intensified calls to identify who ordered the killing.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/brazil-supreme-court-panel-votes-unanimously-to-convict-plotters-of-marielle-francos-assassination'>Brazil Supreme Court panel convicts plotters of Marielle Franco&#x27;s assassination</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4g058v3d35o'>Politician brothers convicted in Brazil for ordering murder of prominent councillor</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/25/world/americas/brazil-supreme-court-verdict-marielle-franco-murder.html'>Brazil’s Supreme Court Convicts Four Men in Murder of Marielle Franco</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-02-25/marielle-franco-case-brazao-brothers-convicted-of-ordering-murder-of-rio-councilwoman.html'>Marielle Franco case: Brazão brothers convicted of ordering murder of Rio councilwoman</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/25/brazil-politician-brothers-convicted-murder'>Brazilian politician brothers convicted of ordering murder of Rio city councillor</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/02/26/brazil-braz-o-brothers-sentenced-to-76-years-for-ordering-marielle-franco-killing'>Brazil: Brazão brothers sentenced to 76 years for ordering Marielle Franco killing</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/26/brazils-supreme-court-imposes-steep-sentences-for-marielle-franco-murder'>Brazil’s Supreme Court imposes steep sentences for Marielle Franco murder</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260225-brazil-politicians-convicted-for-ordering-murder-of-black-activist-councilor'>The Supreme Federal Court of Brazil sentences former Rio de Janeiro legislators Chiquinho and Domingos Brazão to 76 years and three months in prison each for ordering the 2018 killing of city councilor Marielle Franco and her driver, convicting them of double aggravated homicide, participation in an armed criminal organization, and attempted murder.</a> - france24.com</li></ul>